<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indus Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> Valley is the region along the Indus River in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> it was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus-valley-civilisation">Indus Valley Civilisation</a>, known to Mesopotamians as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meluhha">Meluhha</a>. It was linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> through maritime trade via the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>.</p></div>
